            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-20920",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "nodejs-handlebars: lookup helper fails to properly validate templates allowing for arbitrary JavaScript execution"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Handlebars before 3.0.8 and 4.x before 4.5.3 is vulnerable to Arbitrary Code Execution. The lookup helper fails to properly validate templates, allowing attackers to submit templates that execute arbitrary JavaScript. This can be used to run arbitrary code on a server processing Handlebars templates or in a victim's browser (effectively serving as XSS)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-20920",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-20920\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: handlebars\nFixed Version: 3.0.8, 4.5.3\nLink: [CVE-2019-20920](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-20920)\nHandlebars before 3.0.8 and 4.x before 4.5.3 is vulnerable to Arbitrary Code Execution. The lookup helper fails to properly validate templates, allowing attackers to submit templates that execute arbitrary JavaScript. This can be used to run arbitrary code on a server processing Handlebars templates or in a victim's browser (effectively serving as XSS).",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-20920**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|handlebars|3.0.8, 4.5.3|[CVE-2019-20920](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-20920)|\n\nHandlebars before 3.0.8 and 4.x before 4.5.3 is vulnerable to Arbitrary Code Execution. The lookup helper fails to properly validate templates, allowing attackers to submit templates that execute arbitrary JavaScript. This can be used to run arbitrary code on a server processing Handlebars templates or in a victim's browser (effectively serving as XSS)."
