            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-2950",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "lodash: Lodash: Prototype pollution allows deletion of built-in prototype properties via array path bypass"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Impact:\n\nLodash versions 4.17.23 and earlier are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the _.unset and _.omit functions. The fix for (CVE-2025-13465: https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as Object.prototype, Number.prototype, and String.prototype.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\nPatches:\n\nThis issue is patched in 4.18.0.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2950",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-2950\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: lodash-es\nFixed Version: 4.18.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-2950](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2950)\nImpact:\n\nLodash versions 4.17.23 and earlier are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the _.unset and _.omit functions. The fix for (CVE-2025-13465: https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as Object.prototype, Number.prototype, and String.prototype.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\nPatches:\n\nThis issue is patched in 4.18.0.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-2950**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|lodash-es|4.18.0|[CVE-2026-2950](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-2950)|\n\nImpact:\n\nLodash versions 4.17.23 and earlier are vulnerable to prototype pollution in the _.unset and _.omit functions. The fix for (CVE-2025-13465: https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as Object.prototype, Number.prototype, and String.prototype.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\nPatches:\n\nThis issue is patched in 4.18.0.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version."
              },
